WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.130
Two aircraft, drawn as dots, each
trailing a straight dotted path.

2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.810
Seen from above, the paths cross.

3
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.460
That looks like trouble.

4
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.470
But swing the camera round.

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.410
Do the paths really meet
in three dimensions?

6
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.510
And if they do, do the
aircraft get there together?

7
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.070
So, will they collide, or just pass close?

8
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.320
In this mission, you'll write a straight
path as r equals a plus lambda b:

9
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.220
a point plus multiples of a direction.

10
00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:32.580
You'll find that two lines in
three dimensions can cross,

11
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.660
or miss each other completely.

12
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.950
And you'll let the
parameter stand for time,

13
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.610
so each position depends on t.

14
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:44.730
Your mission: decide whether two aircraft
on straight paths will collide or just

15
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.790
pass close.
